# =====================================================================
# FILE: .dockerignore            (REPO ROOT, next to the Dockerfile)
# =====================================================================
# Works like .gitignore, but for Docker. When you run "docker build .",
# Docker first packs the whole folder into a "build context" and sends it
# to the builder. Everything listed here is left out of that package:
#   - faster builds (less to send)
#   - better caching (a changed README does not break the cache)
#   - safer (secrets never get a chance to land inside an image)
# More: docs/docker/02-build-multistage-optimize.md and 03-security.md
# =====================================================================

# Build output - the container builds its own
**/bin/
**/obj/
TestResults/

# Git and CI files - not needed to build the app
.git/
.github/
.gitignore

# SECRETS and local settings - must never end up inside an image
.env*
**/appsettings.Local.json
**/appsettings.example.json

# Editor files
.vs/
.idea/
*.user

# Docker's own files and documentation - not part of the app
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose*.yml
docs/
*.md
